                <pb facs="0136" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Conference/143: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-31T14:00:00-05:00">October 31, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>433. Your 681, October 30, 9 p.m. No approach resembling that made by Yoshida to
                    you and reported in your first paragraph, has been made either by the Japanese
                    Foreign Office or the Japanese Ambassador here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
